Depression Scale (HADS), for Big-Five personality dimensions using the Ten-Item Personality Inventory (TIPI), and for 
vulnerability to stress using the Stress Vulnerability Scale (SVS). RESULTS Symptoms of anxiety and symptoms of 
depression were prevalent in medical students (43% and 14%, respectively) and in humanities students (52% and 12%, 
respectively). In medical students the score on the HADS anxiety subscale and the score on the HADS depression subscale 
correlated negatively with the score on the TIPI Emotional Stability scale (r = -0.39, p < 0.01 and r = -0.2, p < 0.01, 
respectively) and correlated positively with the score on the SVS (r = 0.38, p < 0.01 and r = 0.44, p < 0.01, 
